  "original_observations": [
    "Each actual installed run called one indexed cursor-backed HistoryScan. Legacy miner, silo detector, SZZ, metrics metadata and behavioral projection received that same scan. An independent full-traversal fallback was forbidden and no fallback occurred.",
    "Observed Git revision traversals and per-commit diffs were cold 1/9, warm 0/0, fresh 1/9, raw traversal bound 1/2, and raw record bound 1/8. Warm reused all nine valid records. Retained file metrics and silo results agree across cold, warm and fresh with only the analysis timestamp omitted, and the entire behavioral JSON is byte-identical.",
    "Every case executes one whole-parent blame on the same selected parent. The SZZ limit is 1 and the cap warning appears only when a second eligible fix remains. The separately configured behavioral cap selects three accepted commits or two under the raw traversal cap. The raw cap and its partial outcome are visible in raw, legacy and behavioral documents.",
    "The 1,024-byte cap refused the single 2,268-byte commit before its diff. Nine selected positions yielded eight valid raw rows and one 320-byte unavailable row in the checked SQLite view. selected_records_complete is false and raw, legacy and behavioral reports retain the exact refusal.",
    "Actual repository inventory was unchanged across the five cases. I independently matched the Git commit, tree and blob objects to their preregistered bytes, all selected record digests and ordered cache checkpoint links, actual output hashes, the unchanged source file and exact four source JUnit cases. Source and installed phases and B11 wrapper all exited 0."
  ],
